From: xinkev <xinkev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fog: make adb over USB work (32-bit DWC3 DMA + PHY rails)

Applies on top of the upstream Redmi10c patch (20260813 or 20260831).
Root cause: DWC3 GHWPARAMS0 reports AWIDTH=64, so the driver sets a
64-bit DMA mask and the event ring lands above 4 GiB (GEVNTADRHI=1).
This USB master cannot write there: every endpoint event reads back
as zero ('unknown endpoint event 0'), ep0 never completes, and the
host never enumerates. Forcing 32-bit coherent DMA moves the ring to
0x43800000; the storm drops to 0 and adb enumerates.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -2288,11 +2288,27 @@
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, dwc);
 	dwc3_cache_hwparams(dwc);
 
-	if (!dev_is_pci(dwc->sysdev) &&
-	    DWC3_GHWPARAMS0_AWIDTH(dwc->hwparams.hwparams0) == 64) {
-		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
-		if (ret)
-			goto err_disable_clks;
+	if (!dev_is_pci(dwc->sysdev)) {
+		u64 dma_mask = 0;
+
+		/*
+		 * Some Qualcomm integrations report a 64-bit AWIDTH but only
+		 * forward/implement 32 address bits on the USB master. Event
+		 * ring and TRB pools then land above 4 GiB, the controller's
+		 * writes never reach them, and every event reads back as zero
+		 * ("unknown endpoint event 0", no enumeration). Let the board
+		 * DT force 32-bit coherent allocations in that case.
+		 */
+		if (of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "snps,force-32bit-dma"))
+			dma_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(32);
+		else if (DWC3_GHWPARAMS0_AWIDTH(dwc->hwparams.hwparams0) == 64)
+			dma_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(64);
+
+		if (dma_mask) {
+			ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev, dma_mask);
+			if (ret)
+				goto err_disable_clks;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/*
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-fog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-fog.dts
@@ -66,8 +66,51 @@
 	status = "okay";
 	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	maximum-speed = "high-speed";
+	/*
+	 * GHWPARAMS0 reports AWIDTH=64, but coherent buffers allocated above
+	 * 4 GiB were never written by the controller (event ring read back as
+	 * all-zero; GEVNTADRHI=1). Force 32-bit DMA so the event ring/TRBs
+	 * stay in the address range the USB master can actually reach.
+	 */
+	snps,force-32bit-dma;
 };
 
+/*
+ * Real Khaje USB rails + PHY reset. The board needs L4/L12/L15 powered
+ * (the upstream dummy vregs leave the PHY without its 0.88 V core rail)
+ * and GCC_QUSB2PHY_PRIM_BCR deasserted, or the PHY never drives D+.
+ *
+ * cfg_ahb is deliberately absent: the USB clocks are protected in the
+ * GCC node, so gcc-sm6115 never registers GCC_AHB2PHY_USB_CLK. The femto
+ * driver force-enables it via MMIO (force_usb_clks), as upstream does.
+ * Do not add cfg_ahb back without removing the protected-clocks list —
+ * clk_get() on a protected clock returns NULL and the PHY loses the bus.
+ */
+&usb_hsphy {
+	clocks = <&xo_board>;
+	clock-names = "ref";
+	resets = <&gcc GCC_QUSB2PHY_PRIM_BCR>;
+	/*
+	 * Supply map from this phone's downstream DT (pbrp-live.dtb hsphy):
+	 *   vdd     = pm6125_l4  @ 0.88 V  -> mainline "vdda-pll"
+	 *   vdda18  = pm6125_l12 @ 1.80 V  -> mainline "vdda18"
+	 *   vdda33  = pm6125_l15 @ 3.23 V  -> mainline "vdda33"
+	 * The author's patch bound BOTH vdda-pll and vdda18 to l12, leaving
+	 * the 0.88 V core rail unpowered. With every digital setting correct
+	 * (GCTL=device, DCTL running, QSCRATCH VBUS override, event ring up)
+	 * the controller still reported DSTS=USBLNKST 3 (disconnected):
+	 * the PHY could not drive the D+ pullup without that rail.
+	 * l4 is shared with the UFS PHY and already pinned 880 mV.
+	 */
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&pm6125_l4a>;
+	vdda18-supply = <&pm6125_l12a>;
+	vdda33-supply = <&pm6125_l15a>;
+	/* Khaje line tuning, verbatim from this phone's downstream DT
+	 * (pbrp-live.dtb hsphy, panel variant). Applied by the patched
+	 * femto driver — mainline ignores this property upstream. */
+	qcom,param-override-seq = <0x67 0x6c 0x0f 0x70 0x2c 0x74>;
+};
+
 &pon_pwrkey {
 	status = "okay";
 };
